142 0 obj
  << /ActualText (PapaBite is a father\055centred weaning toolkit that helps new fathers move from passive presence to active caregiver\056 Within the UK parenting and healthcare system\054 care pathways\054 information\054 and decisions tend to default to the mother\054 while fathers are quietly cast as the \042helper\056\042 It isn\047t that fathers don\047t want to be involved\056 They simply lack a clear entry point\054 the right tools\054 and the chance to be seen by their family\056\nWe found that as a baby enters weaning between six and twelve months and depends less on breastfeeding\054 caregiving becomes genuinely open to being shared for the first time\056 Weaning holds a whole chain of concrete tasks\054 from shopping to prep to feeding\054 making it an ideal entry point for a father to step in and build a bond with his child\056\nPapaBite is a toolkit a father can pick up and start using right away\054 one that reframes feeding from a domestic chore into a ritual through which he builds his parenting identity\056 Through weekly challenges\054 a recording book\054 and clear guidance\054 a father is no longer told what to do\056 He is invited to lead real moments of care\054 care that can be practised\054 completed\054 and seen by the whole family\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 143 0 R
     /Pg 136 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

